{
  "content": "For split_tasks, updateMode and tasksRaw are required string arguments. tasksRaw is itself JSON-encoded text: serialize a JSON array of task objects as a string, with normal JSON escaping for quotes, backslashes, and other special characters. Dependencies can be represented by a referenced task's exact name or, when the task already exists, its ID; the resulting dependency is stored as a task-ID reference. The observed split and later note update preserved these dependency links.",
  "applicability": "Use when calling split_tasks to add tasks with prerequisite relationships, including when adding a task that depends on an existing task.",
  "actions": [
    "Provide updateMode as a string and tasksRaw as a string containing valid JSON.",
    "Include dependencies as a JSON array of prerequisite names or existing task IDs.",
    "Escape the JSON text correctly before passing it as the tasksRaw string."
  ],
  "verification": "Observed task listings and task-detail readbacks showed the expected dependency links after splitting and after a subsequent note update. These checks establish the recorded tool effects, not general software correctness."
}
